Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.60,0:00:05.28,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,This man... was the driver of the \Ncarriage that Lady Anastasia rode in.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.24,0:00:08.64,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Was it you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.31,0:00:12.14,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Did you kill Anastasia Shaderan?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.33,0:01:52.65,Episode Title,text,0,0,0,,{\3c&H6E6C70&\fad(446,429)\pos(517,320)}Episode 9 "In Pursuit \Nof Anastasia's Spirit"
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.17,0:01:58.54,Italics,Mio; internal,0,0,0,,As I thought, it doesn't seem \Nlikely he'll simply tell us.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.28,0:02:01.74,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,I've brought him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.84,0:02:07.26,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Johan...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.82,0:02:15.53,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,I've heard you're from the Bandelee \NIslands. I'm from the same area.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.53,0:02:18.03,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,What island were you born on?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.03,0:02:22.70,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,Y-You're Bandeleese? \NWhy are you working in a castle?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.59,0:02:27.52,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,Count Granado's mother is a \Nrefugee from another country.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.52,0:02:31.39,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,He has also grown up suffering insults \Nfrom the people of this kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.39,0:02:34.37,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,He doesn't discriminate.\NI can assure you of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.04,0:02:38.81,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,The master hasn't called \Nyou here to condemn you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.81,0:02:41.12,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,He wants to give you compensation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.12,0:02:41.97,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.57,0:02:45.68,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,Compensation for killing Anastasia.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.44,0:02:49.77,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.77,0:02:52.64,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Johan is lying to try to \Nget the truth from him.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.28,0:02:58.06,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,As the son of a duke, the master was \Nbound to a fiancée through duty,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.06,0:03:02.09,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,but it was her younger sister, Marie,\Nwho stands here, that he fell in love with.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.09,0:03:04.25,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,I'm sure you don't need \Nme to tell you the rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.74,0:03:07.71,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,So the beautiful older sister was in the way.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.10,0:03:12.76,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,Indeed. And so the master would \Nlike to discreetly reward you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.76,0:03:16.83,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,In fact, he may even employ \Nyou here at the castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.22,0:03:23.19,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,And if you were a castle employee, then the \Nowner of the carriage rental couldn't yell at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.19,0:03:27.14,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,Th-That would be too much, wouldn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.91,0:03:39.91,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Please tell us the truth, Jacob.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.26,0:03:44.16,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,That day, the old guy who runs \Nthe shop was really excited.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.60,0:03:48.42,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,Jacob, bring out the best carriage!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.42,0:03:50.28,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,Huh? What's this about?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.28,0:03:52.55,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,The lord's oldest daughter's getting married.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.55,0:03:56.12,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,A job this big doesn't \Ncome around very often.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.88,0:03:59.59,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,Apologies for keeping you waiting, Baron.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.59,0:04:02.88,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,We have prepared our very \Nbest carriage for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.16,0:04:06.58,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,It comes to roughly this amount.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.29,0:04:09.27,Flashback,Gregor,0,0,0,,Ridiculous!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.27,0:04:11.51,Flashback,Gregor,0,0,0,,I will only pay half that much.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.51,0:04:17.60,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,B-But for that amount, we can't manage \Nto provide a decent carriage or inn.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.85,0:04:21.22,Flashback,Gregor,0,0,0,,Figuring out what to do about \Nthat is your job, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.22,0:04:22.98,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,You may say so,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.33,0:04:27.75,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,but the lady getting married is \Nyour darling daughter, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.46,0:04:34.54,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,Jacob, you understand, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.54,0:04:37.55,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,Lay a hand on the lord's daughter \Nand being fired is the least—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.55,0:04:40.52,Flashback,Jaocb,0,0,0,,Yes, yes. I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.52,0:04:42.70,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,But it's strange, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.54,0:04:46.09,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,Unlike that raggedy younger daughter,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.09,0:04:49.36,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,the older one is supposed \Nto be adored, isn't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.19,0:04:52.42,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,That's not for us to worry about!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.42,0:04:54.15,Flashback,shop owner,0,0,0,,Now, would you hurry up?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.52,0:05:06.49,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,Hey, my lady! You're just \Nas pretty as the rumors say!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.49,0:05:09.26,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,I bet you've got your pick of the men, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.26,0:05:11.86,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,Could it be you've actually \Nplayed around a bit?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.86,0:05:16.19,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,Just joking. Sorry for being so crude.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.77,0:05:19.54,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,I'm just a humble hired driver after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.51,0:05:21.81,Flashback,Anastasia,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.81,0:05:24.26,Default,Jacob; present,0,0,0,,Her attitude made me realize,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.72,0:05:28.40,Default,Jacob; present,0,0,0,,the only way she could live was \Nby following her parents' orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.40,0:05:31.08,Default,Jacob; present,0,0,0,,She was a doll with nothing \Nmore than her looks.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.77,0:05:39.63,Default,Jacob; present,0,0,0,,That's how I knew she wouldn't run away.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.27,0:05:42.03,Default,Jacob; present,0,0,0,,No matter what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.10,0:05:52.58,Flashback,Anastasia,0,0,0,,Wh-Why have you stopped the carriage?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.58,0:05:54.29,Flashback,Anastasia,0,0,0,,The royal capital is close, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.29,0:05:56.90,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,We're camping here for the night.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.90,0:05:59.17,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,And the horses are tired from the rain.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.48,0:06:01.75,Flashback,Anastasia,0,0,0,,The river is dangerous, swollen with the rain!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.75,0:06:03.55,Flashback,Anastasia,0,0,0,,Isn't that all the more reason to hurry?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.00,0:06:10.45,Flashback,Anastasia,0,0,0,,I-If you dare lay a hand on the fiancée of \Na count, do you know what will happen to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.45,0:06:12.81,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,I don't, and I don't care.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.06,0:06:17.25,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,When the count discovers that his \Nfiancée was defiled by a foreigner,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.25,0:06:19.95,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,I wonder what'll happen to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.83,0:06:25.15,Default,Jacob; present,0,0,0,,Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.68,0:06:25.50,Default Top,Kyros,0,0,0,,Mio!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.50,0:06:27.00,Default Top,Kyros,0,0,0,,He hasn't finished his story yet!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.01,0:06:27.80,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,What're you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.80,0:06:30.67,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,What? I thought this was what you wanted!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.57,0:06:32.48,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Mio!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.51,0:06:36.71,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,I'll take your place.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.99,0:06:46.23,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,You! Where did you get the hair and clothes \Nfor the doll that's at the baron's house?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.88,0:06:47.71,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,Tell us!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.41,0:06:51.31,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,I-I took the clothes off her myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.31,0:06:52.48,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,And the hair?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.48,0:06:54.47,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,Th-That was...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.09,0:06:57.68,Flashback,Jacob,0,0,0,,Don't move! Just stay still!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.68,0:06:59.85,Flashback,Anastasia,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.19,0:07:04.81,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,She went and cut her own hair off!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.81,0:07:07.57,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,Look! I've still got a scar from it!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.57,0:07:09.28,Default,Tomas,0,0,0,,You got what you deserved!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.82,0:07:13.20,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Wounded, you retrieved the clothes and hair,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.66,0:07:17.27,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,then sold them to Lady Elvira, who was \Nin shock from her daughter's death.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.27,0:07:20.33,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,I-I wasn't planning to sell \Nthem to her from the beginning!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.56,0:07:24.02,Default Top,Jacob,0,0,0,,I heard that the baroness was looking \Nfor materials to make a doll!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.36,0:07:26.97,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,To cover up your own crime, \Nyou destroyed the carriage,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.97,0:07:29.97,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,and lied in your testimony, saying \Nthat you were attacked by bandits.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.97,0:07:33.45,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,That woman fell into the \Nriver! That's the {\i1}truth!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.45,0:07:35.76,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,She was trying to run away and she slipped!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.76,0:07:37.63,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,It was an accident!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.63,0:07:39.43,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,I didn't kill her!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.43,0:07:41.47,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,Please believe me!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.47,0:07:42.73,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,That's enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.10,0:07:44.51,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I don't want to hear any more.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.01,0:07:46.05,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Marie.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.33,0:07:53.82,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,My older sister died because \Nof you, didn't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.58,0:08:04.43,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,B-But, you know? I think it was the right \Nmove not to take that woman as your wife!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.83,0:08:09.13,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,She had men's clothing that didn't \Nfit her hidden away in her bags!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.83,0:08:14.12,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,What a crazy woman! She must've \Nhad men besides her fiancé!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.12,0:08:17.68,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,Even if she had married you, \Nshe'd definitely have cheated on you!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.68,0:08:19.61,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Do not insult my sister!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.80,0:08:29.83,Default,Jacob,0,0,0,,Wh-What? Do you want to get \Nwhat that woman got, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.83,0:08:30.68,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Stop talking!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.93,0:08:41.53,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Sister, I...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.05,0:08:51.08,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry, Lord Kyros.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.08,0:08:54.15,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,No, I'm the one who should apologize.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.74,0:09:00.82,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Until just now, I didn't \Nregret Anastasia's death.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.41,0:09:02.43,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.43,0:09:03.68,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Neither did I.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.54,0:09:06.83,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Mio...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.83,0:09:12.99,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,We thought that Anastasia had tyrannized \Nyou the same way your parents did.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.54,0:09:17.17,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Sh-She didn't! Not even once!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.17,0:09:19.87,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Yes, I understand that now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.87,0:09:21.71,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,That's why I feel so guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.83,0:09:27.23,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I thought that her death \Nwas her divine punishment.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.23,0:09:28.70,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,And that isn't all.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.10,0:09:32.55,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I thought that my mistakenly proposing \Nto her was a stroke of good luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.55,0:09:34.83,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Because of that error, you were safe, Marie.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.83,0:09:36.72,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,That's what I believed.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.59,0:09:41.52,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Truthfully, it should have \Nbeen me in that carriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.52,0:09:44.94,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,My sister was there in my place.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.94,0:09:49.65,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Marie... Will you allow me to \Napologize at Anastasia's grave?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.05,0:09:51.47,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,She doesn't have a grave.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.96,0:09:54.32,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,My father said that a \Ngravestone would be a waste.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.83,0:09:58.19,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Her funeral was terribly plain, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.19,0:10:03.00,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,In the end, my sister's name wasn't \Neven inscribed in the public cemetery.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.48,0:10:06.62,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I'd at least like to offer \Nher spirit some comfort.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.62,0:10:08.92,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Was there a place that Anastasia liked?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.92,0:10:11.22,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Flowers or food? What about a song?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.85,0:10:16.92,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,I didn't know anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.16,0:10:22.79,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,At some point, a huge gulf opened between us.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.46,0:10:27.58,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Me, who always wore tatters, \Nbut could walk freely outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.43,0:10:32.67,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,My sister, who was forced to dress \Nup in a tiny, enclosed garden.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.12,0:10:37.58,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,A perfect being who should be beloved by all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.96,0:10:42.78,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,And I believed that was \Nwhy the gods took her away.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.67,0:10:50.20,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,But even my sister... was just \Na person living her life.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.70,0:10:54.29,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,It's such an obvious thing, \Nbut I'd forgotten that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.76,0:10:57.99,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,All of this is my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.99,0:11:01.75,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I had no right to punch that man.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.86,0:11:04.62,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Neither do I.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.70,0:11:07.22,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Because I...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.92,0:11:10.88,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,I'm just one of the many \Npeople who killed Anastasia.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.31,0:11:19.99,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Rest well, Anastasia.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.31,0:11:28.58,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,This waterway runs all the way to the \Nartisans' quarter in the royal capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.06,0:11:30.79,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,While she was alive,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.79,0:11:34.30,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,my sister once said that she wanted \Nto design clothes in the capital.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.25,0:11:41.47,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,In such a lively place, perhaps \NAnastasia won't feel lonely.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.47,0:11:42.93,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.25,0:11:51.98,Flashback Italics,young Anastasia,0,0,0,,Marie! Let's play!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.67,0:12:00.52,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I hope that's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.95,0:12:10.53,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,It's been a week since then, and the \Natmosphere in the castle has returned to normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.26,0:12:13.83,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Miss Marie is sewing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.55,0:12:17.64,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,And what are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.64,0:12:21.89,Default Top,Kyros,0,0,0,,If Marie pricks her finger on a needle, \NI am here to treat it immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.59,0:12:24.97,Letter Font,text,0,0,0,,{\an8\bord2\3c&HF0F0F0&\pos(306,235)\fs18}Medicine\NBox
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.89,0:12:24.34,Default Top,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,So you're not doing anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.89,0:12:26.50,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,It's finished!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.50,0:12:30.17,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Lord Kyros, I'm going to \Nuse your hair for a moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.47,0:12:31.57,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Of course!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.30,0:12:35.27,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,M-My son has turned into a faithful dog.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.51,0:12:34.60,Default Top,Marie; background,0,0,0,,Please face the other way.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.60,0:12:35.54,Default Top,Kyros; background,0,0,0,,Like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.54,0:12:37.15,Default Top,Marie; background,0,0,0,,Oh, now if you'll face forward.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.11,0:12:42.31,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Your hair is so beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.89,0:12:48.79,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Marie, your fingers move in such a \Ncharming manner. It feels very nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.69,0:12:52.62,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,You're both so innocent!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.62,0:12:55.03,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Like a couple who are \Neach others' first loves!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.03,0:12:56.59,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,You're right. What of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.08,0:13:00.01,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,So much happened that my giving \Nthese to you has been delayed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.01,0:13:02.30,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,They're gifts for you from the market!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.87,0:13:05.77,Default,Tunika,0,0,0,,Oh, thank you so much!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.77,0:13:07.18,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,How beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.86,0:13:09.32,Default Top,Tunika; background,0,0,0,,It's adorable, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.02,0:13:10.10,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Lady Marie.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.32,0:13:10.91,Default Top,Liu Liu; background,0,0,0,,Yes, it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.52,0:13:13.48,Default Top,Mio,0,0,0,,Souvenirs may be \Nthe true pleasure of travel,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.48,0:13:16.54,Default Top,Mio,0,0,0,,but I believe that spending money \Nand effort on me is a waste of—
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.86,0:13:17.44,Default,Tunika,0,0,0,,Enough! Just accept her gift!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.44,0:13:25.24,Default,text,0,0,0,,{\an9\fs16\fnArial\bord2\shad0\c&H4D5457&\3c&HF6FCFD&\b1\pos(625,15)}Poke Poke Poke Poke Poke Poke
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.73,0:13:21.82,Default,Tunika,0,0,0,,You should just be happy \Nand shout with joy like me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.82,0:13:25.23,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I-I'm sorry! I didn't mean to force it on you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.77,0:13:29.67,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,I accept.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.67,0:13:31.87,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Thank you, Lady Marie.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.81,0:13:36.29,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Thank you for everything \Nyou do. I love you, Mio!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:41.72,0:13:45.72,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Since you arrived, Miss Marie,\Neveryone's attitudes have changed a little.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.72,0:13:47.93,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Have they?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.43,0:13:49.92,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,And for you, Marie...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.92,0:13:51.94,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,I have a gift as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.17,0:13:55.39,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Tale of the Raggedy Red Cat{\i0}!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.77,0:13:57.64,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,It's been mended so beautifully!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.64,0:14:00.51,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Since you were going to \Nmend it yourself before...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.72,0:14:06.37,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,This book is full of memories of \Nmy sister. It's very dear to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.13,0:14:08.91,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.34,0:14:11.72,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,I'm just glad you like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.72,0:14:12.96,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,And there's this, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.64,0:14:15.89,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,"Eminent Figures Around the World"?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.89,0:14:17.57,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I requested that one.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.46,0:14:23.29,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,This is Baron Shaderan's mother, and \Nyour grandmother, Marie. Sasha Tillich.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.69,0:14:25.87,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,My grandmother when she was young.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.87,0:14:29.64,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Marie, you told me that Anastasia \Nlooked just like her.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.95,0:14:33.92,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I thought this might help to capture \Nher likeness in a portrait.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.81,0:14:37.73,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Thank you, Lord Kyros.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.10,0:14:40.99,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,So, your older sister took \Nafter your grandmother.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.99,0:14:42.61,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Do you take after your mother?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.90,0:14:46.00,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,In my height and facial features, yes,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.00,0:14:50.03,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,but my mother is blonde.\NI'm the only one with red hair.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.50,0:14:54.67,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Red hair will bring ruin upon \Na house, so I was shunned.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.67,0:14:59.98,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,{\i1}What?!{\i0} There are still people who believe \Nsuch an old-fashioned superstition?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.98,0:15:00.92,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Yes, agreed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.19,0:15:04.52,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,But why is my grandmother in \Na record of eminent people?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.52,0:15:08.14,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,My! You're related, but you haven't \Nheard of Sasha the Heroine?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.14,0:15:09.11,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,She's quite famous.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.11,0:15:10.10,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.76,0:15:15.00,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Despite being born during the war, \Nwhen women had no real status,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.00,0:15:18.18,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,when she was merely eighteen,\Nshe became a military interpreter,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.18,0:15:20.44,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,commanding seven languages. A true genius.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.75,0:15:25.22,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Your grandmother revolutionized the \Nway that women advance in society.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.22,0:15:26.95,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,She did?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.20,0:15:30.69,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,The likes of your father may \Nhave a bit of a complex.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.69,0:15:33.07,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,She'd have been strict \Nabout his education.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.48,0:15:38.22,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I'm not sure about that. My father didn't \Ninteract with my grandmother very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.22,0:15:40.87,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,There may have been some \Ndiscord between them.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.46,0:15:44.33,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,About Baron Shaderan...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.92,0:15:47.37,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,We sent an invitation \Nto the betrothal ceremony,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.37,0:15:48.55,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,but received no reply.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.96,0:15:50.62,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What? That can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.62,0:15:54.52,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,The primary concern is that we have \Nno way of knowing if he'll attend.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.90,0:15:57.81,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,The one who brought Marie here was \Nnone other than the Baron.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.29,0:16:01.51,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Why would he oppose the marriage now?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.04,0:16:06.68,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I don't think my parents \Never meant for me to marry.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.31,0:16:12.77,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,If I could offer one night's comfort, then we \Nwouldn't have to return my sister's betrothal gifts.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.77,0:16:13.74,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Still...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.33,0:16:17.26,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,If he gains connections to \Na ducal house through this marriage,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.26,0:16:19.29,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,his own standing will rise significantly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.64,0:16:22.51,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,No matter how hard a worker you are, Marie...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.51,0:16:23.79,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,Perhaps...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.12,0:16:28.71,Default,Mio,0,0,0,,it's because Lady Marie was doing important \Nwork that he can't entrust to an outsider.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.43,0:16:35.69,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,But I was only doing simple things that \NI learned from my grandmother as a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.29,0:16:41.97,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Your grandmother worked as the lord of the \Nland in the previous baron's stead, didn't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.25,0:16:43.79,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Y-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.79,0:16:50.19,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I heard that the formalities involved in \Nacting as the local lord were difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.19,0:16:53.23,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,And your grandmother and your father,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.54,0:16:56.87,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,the current Baron Shaderan, \Nhad discord between them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.87,0:17:01.95,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Before, you told me that you wrote letters \Non the lord's behalf, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.52,0:17:05.31,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Can your father read and write in Flarian?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.31,0:17:08.75,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Yes, of course! I believe he can.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.99,0:17:11.54,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,Have you ever actually \Nseen him use the language?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.19,0:17:16.09,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Now that you mention it, I haven't.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.09,0:17:18.77,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,But it's impossible that he can't speak it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.77,0:17:20.96,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Flarian is the communal \Nlanguage of the nobility.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.28,0:17:24.67,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,If he couldn't speak it, he wouldn't be \Nable to fulfill his duties as the lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.20,0:17:26.36,Default,Liu Liu,0,0,0,,I knew it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.66,0:17:28.85,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,It can't be. I don't believe it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.41,0:17:31.24,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.56,0:17:35.82,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Mio, send the House of \NShaderan a mandatory summons.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.82,0:17:36.80,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.80,0:17:38.72,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,If they won't respond to that either,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.72,0:17:40.71,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,we'll have to take them \Nto trial in the kingdom's court.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.99,0:17:45.11,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Marie. I wanted to settle \Nthis as peacefully as possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.11,0:17:46.84,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.52,0:17:51.17,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,What has my father done?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.67,0:17:56.01,Default,text,0,0,0,,{\fad(444,1)\shad0\fs30\fnTimes New Roman\c&H475E61&\3c&HDBF1F7&\pos(497,38)}Four Days Later
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.54,0:18:00.38,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Marie.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.98,0:18:15.23,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Hey, everyone! It's the prince everyone \Nloves, Luiphon Sandhalkia Diltz!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.75,0:18:18.34,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Why is it you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.94,0:18:22.91,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Darling Mio, you love to roughhouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.91,0:18:24.58,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Enough of that. Eat before it gets cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.03,0:18:28.77,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,This is delicious!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.77,0:18:31.41,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,I should expect no less of \Nthe chef of Granado Castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.41,0:18:33.80,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,I'd love to have him at the royal—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.32,0:18:36.22,Default,Toppo,0,0,0,,You're too kind, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.22,0:18:39.58,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,He's slimmed down quite a bit, hasn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.22,0:18:43.33,Default,Toppo,0,0,0,,The betrothal ceremony will \Nbe attended by royalty,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.33,0:18:45.80,Default,Toppo,0,0,0,,nobles, and commoners from \Nmany countries, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.80,0:18:50.05,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Oh, I see. You've been incredibly busy \Ndeveloping recipes and sourcing ingredients.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.05,0:18:52.72,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Toppo, don't push yourself too hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.25,0:18:54.56,Default,Toppo,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.56,0:18:57.90,Default,Toppo,0,0,0,,All of this is what I, Toppo, wish to \Ncreate, so I'm more fired up than ever!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.36,0:18:59.45,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Toppo.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.88,0:19:04.61,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Kyros, you really have the \Nbest luck with your servants.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.61,0:19:08.20,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Yes. But more importantly, \Nwhat brings you here today?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.34,0:19:10.84,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Actually...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.66,0:19:15.62,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Your engagement ring.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.01,0:19:19.85,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,I came to check the sizing before \Nthe stone is secured in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.85,0:19:22.12,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Now, dear Marie, hold out your hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.58,0:19:24.02,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Stop right there!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.02,0:19:24.73,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.73,0:19:26.97,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,I'm just checking the size.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.97,0:19:30.63,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,No! Not even just to check the \Nsize! Go away for a minute!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.63,0:19:31.90,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Yes, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.74,0:19:37.16,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,May I check the size?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.16,0:19:38.06,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.06,0:19:41.77,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,The stone isn't set in place yet, so \Nplease don't move your hand too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.82,0:19:48.38,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,It's perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.38,0:19:51.78,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I didn't know that a ring \Ncould feel this nice to wear.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:51.78,0:19:54.41,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,You haven't worn a ring before?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.78,0:19:55.80,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I haven't.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.38,0:19:59.34,Italics,Kyros; internal,0,0,0,,I'm so glad I stopped Luiphon!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.88,0:20:04.07,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Lord Kyros looked for a stone \Nto match the color of my hair.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.07,0:20:08.39,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,This ring really was made just for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.50,0:20:14.79,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Marie...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.79,0:20:16.61,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.19,0:20:21.41,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,The fact that my first ring is a \Ngift from you makes me truly happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.66,0:20:27.60,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I love you, Marie.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.09,0:20:30.17,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I love you from the bottom of my heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.57,0:20:31.63,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,I feel the same!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.70,0:20:34.79,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,More than anyone else in the world...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.02,0:20:37.63,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,it's you that I...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.40,0:20:41.56,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Hey! Are you done yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.97,0:20:46.14,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,So, what do you think of it?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.14,0:20:48.83,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Th-The workmanship is wonderful.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.83,0:20:53.35,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I thought that the only artisan capable \Nof this kind of work was Norman.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.35,0:20:57.68,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Are you referring to the \Nbutton artisan Smith Norman?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.68,0:20:58.48,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.48,0:21:03.41,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,I know he's elderly, but it's \Na shame that he retired.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.41,0:21:05.69,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,He really had amazing skills.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.69,0:21:08.53,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,He was a button maker who also made rings?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.53,0:21:11.57,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Buttons were originally a \Ntype of valuable jewelry.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.20,0:21:14.65,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Being particular about them shows \Ncare in one's appearance.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.65,0:21:17.70,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Sometimes clothes are even made \Nto match a set of buttons.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.58,0:21:20.30,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Oh, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.30,0:21:26.85,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Indeed. The only one capable of executing \Nthe design of that ring may be that Norman.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.85,0:21:27.61,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.06,0:21:32.02,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,You don't mean... Smith \NNorman himself made this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.53,0:21:37.37,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,That's right! It's my real gift to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.37,0:21:40.17,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,I went to him in his retirement \Nand begged, I'll have you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.17,0:21:41.18,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Me, of all people.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.18,0:21:43.40,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,No wonder!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.68,0:21:46.37,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,Thank you, Prince Luiphon.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.37,0:21:50.99,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,But Norman is famous for being stubborn. \NI'm amazed that you convinced him.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.99,0:21:55.61,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,He seemed to have taken on a new apprentice, \Nso perhaps he's had a change of heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.61,0:21:56.78,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Apprentice?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.78,0:22:00.47,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,Yes. Apparently, he's taken in \Na foundling or street urchin.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.81,0:22:03.35,Default,Luiphon,0,0,0,,It happened three months ago in the \Nroyal capital's artisans' quarter.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.62,0:22:04.60,Default,Marie,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.92,0:22:06.39,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,A foundling?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.39,0:22:09.31,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,If they were from outside the capital, \Nwas it a farmer's child?\N
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.31,0:22:12.93,Default,Kyros,0,0,0,,Regional disparities are a problem for the \Nroyal government, aren't they, Prince Luiphon?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.16,0:22:14.56,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,Three months ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.59,0:22:19.81,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,The royal capital's artisans' quarter...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.51,0:22:24.91,Italics,Marie; internal,0,0,0,,{\fad(1,859)}That's... It can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.47,0:24:00.22,Default Top,Tunika,0,0,0,,Our lady is beautiful,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.22,0:24:04.99,Default Top,Tunika,0,0,0,,but when it comes to her older \Nsister, her face always clouds over.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.38,0:24:08.36,Default Top,Tunika,0,0,0,,Next time, "Please Call Off the Betrothal."
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.29,0:24:12.08,Episode Title,text,0,0,0,,{\3c&H6E6C70&\fad(488,1)\pos(526,322)}Episode 10 "Please Call\NOff the Betrothal"
Dialogue: 0,0:24:08.76,0:24:11.38,Default Top,Tunika,0,0,0,,I'd simply hate it if you didn't watch.
